From c66ed302f9fb7e327f3baa9d549a7d89c1aa0f33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:28:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Trip builder: edit your trip any way you like, and chat to an
 AI to change it

After the quiz a traveller is no longer stuck with what they were given.

On the screen (front end only, ships with the site):
- Undo / Redo (bar above the itinerary, on every toast, Cmd/Ctrl+Z), including after "Start over".
- Add a stop in between any two stops, or at the start; swap a stop for another place.
- The day-by-day plan is editable: move a tour to another day, add a tour to a day, remove one.
  A tour moved to a day is pinned there and survives share links.
- All of it goes through one validated, all-or-nothing editing layer (edit.js).

The AI chat ("Chat to change it"):
- A panel beside the trip (a sheet on phones). The AI looks things up and edits the trip through the same
  editing layer, so it can do nothing a button can't, and every change shows what it changed with an Undo.
- New Edge Function trip-builder-chat: the browser sends only the conversation; the system prompt, tools,
  model and limits are ours. Default model claude-opus-5-5 (TRIP_CHAT_MODEL / TRIP_CHAT_EFFORT to change).
  Needs the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY secret. Without it the function answers 503 and the builder uses its
  built-in quick helper ("remove Hoi An", "add Bangkok for 3 nights"), so shipping this breaks nothing.
- Migration: daily usage counters (per person by salted IP hash, and overall) checked before Claude is called.
- Tested against a fake Claude only: _shared/trip-builder-chat.test.ts (11) and e2e/chat-e2e.ts (37, the real
  builder code against the real handler). Never run against the real API.

See docs/trip-builder-chat.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
